STUDENT(student_id PK, student_name, programme)
LECTURER(lecturer_id PK, lecturer_name)
MODULE(module_code PK, module_title, lecturer_id FK references LECTURER)
ENROLMENT(student_id FK references STUDENT, module_code FK references MODULE, semester, grade, PK(student_id,module_code,semester))

Every determinant is a key in its new table, so all four relations are BCNF. Each given FD is represented directly, hence dependency preserving. Joining ENROLMENT to STUDENT and MODULE on their keys and MODULE to LECTURER on its key is lossless.

